  "identifier": "DTIC_AD0631689",
  "title": "DTIC AD0631689: DEVELOPMENT OF FLEXIBLE PACKAGED BREAD -TYPE PRODUCTS INCLUDING BREAD: PHASE I AND II. SINGLE AND MULTIPLE STAGE PROCESSING METHODS",
  "creator": "Defense Technical Information Center",
  "year": 1966,
  "subject": [
    "DTIC Archive",
    "PILLSBURY MILLS INC MINNEAPOLIS MN",
    "*MILITARY RATIONS",
    "*BREAD",
    "STABILITY",
    "PROCESSING",
    "TASTE",
    "PACKAGING",
    "STERILIZATION"
  ],
  "description": "A white bread type product packaged in a lightweight, flexible pouch was developed. It is palatable, stable, and commercially sterile. Both single and multiple stage processes were explored. Many formulations were tested with the best products obtained with a synthetic flour formula chemically leavened. A steam water retort was used for cooking and sterilizing the bread product. Sterilization values of F sub o = 4 were required for sterility.",
